WEBVTT

00:12:30.003 --> 00:12:33.636
is that every single paper we write,
every project we do,

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:37.820
has exactly the same chance
of being our personal best.

00:12:37.844 --> 00:12:42.797
That is, discovery is like
a lottery ticket.

00:12:42.821 --> 00:12:45.172
And the more lottery tickets we buy,

00:12:45.196 --> 00:12:46.703
the higher our chances.

00:12:46.727 --> 00:12:48.286
And it happens to be so

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:51.029
that most scientists buy
most of their lottery tickets

00:12:51.053 --> 00:12:53.513
in the first 10, 15 years of their career,

00:12:53.537 --> 00:12:56.950
and after that,
their productivity decreases.

00:12:57.411 --> 00:12:59.495
They're not buying
any more lottery tickets.

00:12:59.519 --> 00:13:02.963
So it looks as if
they would not be creative.